### PART 9 – Authoritative forensic learning resources

These are useful starting points for studying forensic methodology and practical investigations.

* [NIST Digital Investigation Techniques](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ir/2022/NIST.IR.8354.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com) – scientific foundations of digital investigation.

* [Open University Digital Forensics](https://www.open.edu/openlearn/mod/oucontent/view.php?id=31361&section=4.3&utm_source=chatgpt.com) – introduction to forensic specialisations.

* [DHS Digital Forensics Tools](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/publications/Digital-Forensics-Tools-TN_0716-508.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com) – forensic tools and evidence collection.

* [IBM Digital Forensics](https://www.ibm.com/think/topics/digital-forensics?utm_source=chatgpt.com) – branches and applications of digital forensics.

* [Digital Forensics Subdomains Research](https://pure.port.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/94821476/Digital_forensics_subdomains.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com) – academic overview of specialist forensic fields.

### My recommendation for your offensive security career

Learn the relationship between three disciplines:

Offensive security

Discover and validate security weaknesses.

Digital forensics

Understand what happened and establish evidence.

Incident response

Contain threats and restore secure operations.

An exceptional security researcher should understand not only how a vulnerability is discovered, but also how to reconstruct the events, identify the affected components, preserve evidence and verify the impact.

One important distinction: The 30 areas above are a comprehensive learning taxonomy, not an official universal list. Some overlap or are sub-specialisations of others; professional investigations frequently combine multiple branches. Pure Portsmouth +2

My suggested next step is to study Computer Forensics from absolute beginner to advanced, including its theory, commands, tools, practical investigations and Python automation, before moving to memory and network forensics.
